.TH AL-FALAK 1 "October 2026" "al-falak" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
al-falak \- Islamic astronomy: prayer times, Qibla, Sunnah markers, Hijri dates, moon sighting, ephemeris
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B al-falak
.RI < prayer " | " qibla " | " sunnah " | " hijri " | " moon-sighting " | " astro >
.RI [ options "] [" --json ]
.br
.B "al-falak astro"
.RI < lunar-position " | " delta-t >
.RI [ options "] [" --json ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B al-falak
is the command-line interface of the al-falak Islamic astronomy library.
Every invocation names one explicit subcommand; a bare invocation with no
subcommand is an error. Every subcommand accepts
.B --json
to emit the same keys as one compact JSON object instead of
.I key=value
lines. Datetimes print as ISO-8601 with offset (UTC by default, or
.B --timezone
where supported). Floats print with full precision in text
.RI ( nan
lowercase, except
.B qibla
which prints direction to 6 decimals and distance to 3)
and as
.I null
in JSON; booleans print lowercase in text.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS prayer
Print prayer times (imsak, fajr, sunrise, syuruk, ishraq, dhuha, dhuhr,
asr, maghrib, isha), one
.I name=ISO-8601
line per marker in chronological order.
.PP
.RS
.nf
al-falak prayer --latitude 35.7750 --longitude -78.6336 \\
    --date 2015-07-12 --method NORTH_AMERICA
.fi
.RE
.TP
.BR --latitude " / " --lat
(required) Latitude, \-90 to 90.
.TP
.BR --longitude " / " --lon
(required) Longitude, \-180 to 180.
.TP
.B --date DATE
Calendar date as YYYY-MM-DD (default: today, UTC).
.TP
.B --method NAME
Calculation method (default: MUSLIM_WORLD_LEAGUE). One of DUBAI, EGYPTIAN,
JAKIM, KARACHI, KUWAIT, MOON_SIGHTING_COMMITTEE, MUSLIM_WORLD_LEAGUE,
NONE, NORTH_AMERICA, QATAR, SINGAPORE, UMM_AL_QURA, UOIF.
.TP
.B --madhab MADHAB
SHAFI (default) or HANAFI.
.TP
.B --high-latitude-rule RULE
MIDDLE_OF_THE_NIGHT (default), SEVENTH_OF_THE_NIGHT, or TWILIGHT_ANGLE.
.TP
.B --polar-rule RULE
NONE, NEAREST_LATITUDE (default), NEAREST_DAY, or MAKKAH.
.TP
.B --fajr-angle DEG
Override the method's Fajr angle (default: from method).
.TP
.B --isha-angle DEG
Override the method's Isha angle (default: from method).
.TP
.B --isha-interval MIN
Override the method's Isha interval in minutes (default: from method).
.TP
.B --imsak-offset MIN
Minutes before Fajr for Imsak (default: 10).
.TP
.B --ishraq-offset MIN
Minutes after sunrise for Ishraq (default: 15).
.TP
.B --dhuha-offset MIN
Minutes after sunrise for the start of the Dhuha window (default: 28).
.TP
.B --elevation METRES
Observer eye height in metres, dip correction (default: 0.0).
.TP
.B --ramadan
Umm al-Qura Ramadan mode (120 min Isha total; preset only). Off by default.
.TP
.B --timezone NAME
IANA timezone name for display, e.g. Asia/Kuala_Lumpur (default: UTC).
.TP
.B --adjust NAME=MIN
Repeatable per-prayer minute offset; NAME in
imsak,fajr,sunrise,dhuhr,asr,maghrib,isha,ishraq,dhuha (no syuruk slot by
design \(em sunrise flows through). Negatives need the
.I =
form:
.BR "--adjust isha=-1" .
A leading
.I +
is also accepted
.BR ( "--adjust fajr=+2" ).
Magnitude is capped at 1000000 minutes; larger values are rejected.
.TP
.B --json
Emit one compact JSON object instead of
.I key=value
lines.
.SS qibla
Print Qibla direction and distance.
.PP
.RS
.nf
al-falak qibla --latitude 35.7750 --longitude -78.6336 --method ellipsoidal
.fi
.RE
.PP
Text prints the direction to 6 decimals and the distance to 3 decimals;
.B --json
carries the raw floats. With
.BR --declination ,
a fourth
.I magnetic=
line (compass heading) is added.
.TP
.BR --latitude " / " --lat
(required) Latitude, \-90 to 90.
.TP
.BR --longitude " / " --lon
(required) Longitude, \-180 to 180.
.TP
.B --method MODEL
Earth model: spherical (default) or ellipsoidal (WGS84 geodesic).
.TP
.B --declination DEG
Local magnetic declination in degrees, positive east of true north
(negative west); also prints
.IR magnetic= .
.TP
.B --json
Emit one compact JSON object instead of
.I key=value
lines.
.SS sunnah
Print Sunnah night markers (middle_of_the_night, first_third_of_the_night,
last_third_of_the_night, tahajjud_start, tahajjud_end). Accepts all
.B prayer
location and parameter flags
.RB ( --latitude / --longitude ,
.BR --date ,
.BR --method ,
.BR --madhab ,
.BR --high-latitude-rule ,
.BR --polar-rule ,
.BR --fajr-angle ,
.BR --isha-angle ,
.BR --isha-interval ,
.BR --imsak-offset ,
.BR --ishraq-offset ,
.BR --dhuha-offset ,
.BR --elevation ,
.BR --ramadan ,
.BR --timezone ,
.BR --adjust ),
with the same names and defaults, plus:
.TP
.B --fraction F
Night fraction in the open interval (0, 1); prints a single
.I night_fraction=
line instead of the default marker block.
.TP
.B --start ISO
Custom night-start anchor as an ISO datetime with timezone offset (requires
.BR --fraction ;
default: Maghrib). Must be timezone-aware; naive values are rejected.
Rejected without
.BR --fraction .
.TP
.B --end ISO
Custom night-end anchor as an ISO datetime with timezone offset (requires
.BR --fraction ;
default: next-day Fajr). Must be timezone-aware; naive values are rejected.
Rejected without
.BR --fraction .
.TP
.B --json
Emit one compact JSON object instead of
.I key=value
lines.
.SS hijri
Convert a Gregorian date to a Hijri date (forward), a Hijri date back to
Gregorian
.RB ( --reverse ),
or print a Hijri month length
.RB ( --month-length ).
.PP
.RS
.nf
al-falak hijri --date 2025-03-01 --calendar tabular
al-falak hijri --reverse 1446-09-01 --calendar tabular
al-falak hijri --month-length 1446-09 --calendar tabular
.fi
.RE
.TP
.B --date DATE
Gregorian date as YYYY-MM-DD, forward mode (default: today, UTC). Naive,
treated as UTC.
.TP
.B --calendar RULE
(required) Hijri calendar rule: tabular, uqu, or mabims.
.TP
.B --country CODE
MABIMS country: MY, ID, BN, or SG (case-insensitive; required with
.BR "--calendar mabims" ,
rejected otherwise).
.TP
.B --adjustment-days N
Tabular day shift in [\-2, 2] (default: 0; only with
.BR "--calendar tabular" ).
.TP
.B --sunset-transition
Roll the Hijri day over at Maghrib (requires
.BR --lat / --lon / --time ).
Off by default.
.TP
.B --lat LAT
Observer latitude for sunset rollover (rejected without
.BR --sunset-transition ).
.TP
.B --lon LON
Observer longitude for sunset rollover (rejected without
.BR --sunset-transition ).
.TP
.B --time TIME
Wall-clock time as HH:MM[:SS] on
.BR --date ;
naive, treated as UTC (requires
.BR --sunset-transition ).
.TP
.B --offsets FILE
JSON offset file ({YYYY-MM: shift}) applied last (forward mode only).
.TP
.B --reverse HIJRI-DATE
Hijri date as YYYY-MM-DD; convert back to a Gregorian date (mutually
exclusive with
.BR --date / --sunset-transition / --offsets ;
.B --adjustment-days
allowed with
.BR "--calendar tabular" ).
.TP
.B --month-length YYYY-MM
Hijri year-month; print the month length (29 or 30; mutually exclusive
with
.BR --date / --sunset-transition / --offsets / --adjustment-days ).
.TP
.B --json
Emit one compact JSON object instead of
.I key=value
lines.
.SS moon-sighting
Print crescent geometry and visibility scores (Yallop zone, Odeh class,
and the two MABIMS booleans).
.PP
.RS
.nf
al-falak moon-sighting --latitude 3.1390 --longitude 101.6869 \\
    --date 2025-02-28
.fi
.RE
.PP
In JSON, non-finite floats (e.g. NaN lag when no moonset occurs) become
.IR null .
.TP
.BR --latitude " / " --lat
(required) Latitude, \-90 to 90.
.TP
.BR --longitude " / " --lon
(required) Longitude, \-180 to 180.
.TP
.B --date DATE
(required) Crescent evening as YYYY-MM-DD. No default \(em an explicit
evening is required.
.TP
.B --delta-t-override SEC
Delta-T override in seconds for the TT conversion (default: built-in
polynomial).
.TP
.B --json
Emit one compact JSON object instead of
.I key=value
lines.
.SS astro
Low-level lookups behind one nested subcommand: lunar position or
Delta-T.
.PP
.RS
.nf
al-falak astro delta-t --year 2025.5
al-falak astro lunar-position --julian-day 2460000.5
.fi
.RE
.TP
.B lunar-position --julian-day JD
(required) Julian Day in Terrestrial Time, e.g. 2460000.5. Prints
longitude, latitude, distance_km, right_ascension, declination.
.TP
.B lunar-position --json
Emit one compact JSON object instead of
.I key=value
lines.
.TP
.B delta-t --year YEAR
(required) Decimal year, e.g. 2025.5. Prints
.IR delta_t= .
.TP
.B delta-t --override SEC
Delta-T override in seconds, e.g. an IERS observed value.
.TP
.B delta-t --json
Emit one compact JSON object instead of
.I key=value
lines.
.PP
Years outside 2005\(en2050 emit a
.I UserWarning
to stderr and extrapolate \(em the finite value still prints with exit 0
(an absurd year whose polynomial overflows to non-finite exits 2).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success. Warnings never fail: an out-of-range
.B astro delta-t
year prints a
.I UserWarning
to stderr but the finite value still prints with exit 0 (a non-finite
overflow exits 2).
.TP
.B 2
All user-fixable errors, reported via an argparse error: bad flags and
bad flag values (unknown methods, bad dates/times, unknown timezones,
gate misuse such as a missing
.B --country
with mabims or
.B --time
without
.BR --sunset-transition ,
unreadable
.B --offsets
files, naive
.B --start / --end
anchors or
.B --start / --end
without
.BR --fraction ,
absurd
.B --adjust
magnitudes), out-of-range coordinates and angles, pre-floor dates, polar
day/night with no sunrise/sunset, and moon-sighting evenings with no
sunset. Library
.I ValidationError
(bad user input),
.I ConfigurationError
(inconsistent options), and
.I AstronomicalError
(no sunrise/sunset at this date and latitude) all surface this way.
.SH CAVEATS
The
.B uqu
calendar (1423H Umm al-Qura month-start rule at Makkah, selected with
.BR "hijri --calendar uqu" )
is not the
.B UMM_AL_QURA
prayer preset (Fajr angle / Isha interval given to
.BR "prayer --method UMM_AL_QURA" ),
which only tunes daily prayer times and never converts dates.
.PP
The
.B tabular
calendar is arithmetic and routinely differs from observed
(sighting-based) months by 1\(en2 days \(em never present a tabular date
as an observed date.
.PP
Naive
.B --date
and
.B --time
values are treated as UTC: a local wall-clock time misplaces sunset
rollover by the UTC offset, and
.B sunnah --start / --end
anchors must instead carry an explicit timezone offset (naive anchors are
rejected).
.SH SEE ALSO
Full CLI guide with examples and option tables:
.I docs/user/cli.md
in the al-falak source tree.
